{"title":"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Under_15_seconds)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Under 15 seconds)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following polygons has the largest area?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83ac33b3e3e61ab2ca2c1c80dcbd8766f52066.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(330); int i,j,k; for(i=0;i&lt;5; i=i+1) { for(j=0;j&lt;5;j=j+1) { for(k=0;k&lt;5;k=k+1) { dot((6i+j, k)); }}} draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(3,1)--(3,3)--(2,3)--(2,1)--(1,1)--cycle); draw(shift(6,0)*((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,1)--(3,1)--(3,2)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(0,2)--cycle)); draw(shift(12,0)*((0,1)--(1,0)--(3,2)--(3,3)--(1,1)--(1,3)--(0,4)--cycle)); draw(shift(18,0)*((0,1)--(2,1)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(2,2)--(1,3)--(1,2)--(0,2)--cycle)); draw(shift(24,0)*((1,0)--(2,1)--(2,3)--(3,2)--(3,4)--(0,4)--(1,3)--cycle)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0*6+2, 0), S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (1*6+2, 0), S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (2*6+2, 0), S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (3*6+2, 0), S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, (4*6+2, 0), S);[/asy]\" width=\"552\" height=\"105\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbaaf6e254b88e3be72fd5c3432d53d65785af9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\text{A}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{B}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{C}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{D}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each polygon can be partitioned into unit squares and right triangles with sidelength <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Count the number of boxes enclosed by each polygon, with the unit square being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the triangle being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd6d26513bbf9d11197035fe648afccd8c5d706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.5$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. A has 5, B has 5, C has 5, D has 4.5, and E has 5.5. Therefore, the polygon with the largest area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb4ed349ed3acf64dad610cc8ab55e89d5ecd25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Under_15_seconds.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Under_15_seconds)\">Solution 2 (Under 15 seconds)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Under 15 seconds)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pick's Theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab669894d3001fa5494ffa1bcdaa6e7175c941e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = I + \\frac{1}{2}B - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"127\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the number of lattice points in the interior and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> being the number of lattice points on the boundary.\n</p><p>Ok, so we want to find the polygon with the largest area, first notice that not a single polygon has a lattice point in the interior. Now look at the formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/4471f092a942b7723efe6019da00277dfc780a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2}B - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>So now just look at the polygon with the most lattice points on the boundary, and that is figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5bb2aa78132b4b716cfde4a9136c884d94c753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{E}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" />, with 13 lattice points on the boundary. \nSo the polygon with the largest area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb4ed349ed3acf64dad610cc8ab55e89d5ecd25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~blankbox\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 8\">2002 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"